{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And He saw… and He knew, etc.</b> The meaning: after they cried out and their cry ascended, HaShem remembered the covenant of the patriarchs, and this was the cause for turning to them and seeing them — for the seeing of HaShem upon one who suffers is effective to remove the suffering, for He is compassionate, full of compassions, and His compassions are upon all His works. And this is the meaning of His saying ״וַיֵּדַע״ etc. — in the vernacular, He paid heed. And you will find that in a time of wrath He hides His face, as He said (Deuteronomy 31:18): ״וְאָנֹכִי הַסְתֵּר אַסְתִּיר״ etc. It further intends, in His saying <b>וַיֵּדַע</b>, hidden things that they had done kindly [for one another]."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {0 "The vernacular gloss בְּלַעַ״ז אפיאד״ו renders a Romance (Judaeo-Spanish/Judeo-Arabic) phrase meaning 'He paid heed' or 'He took notice'; transliterated as found."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:23:45.901012048Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}